  "notes": [
    "Transcribed from the scanned MoPA notification dated 05 November 2026 (20 Kartik 1433). Bangla names are verbatim from the notice; English names are conventional translations.",
    "The Cabinet approved the 2027 holiday list on 2026-11-02; the notification was issued on 2026-11-05.",
    "Entries marked with an asterisk in the notice are recorded with dateStatus 'tentative': they depend on moon sighting (or, for Buddhist festivals, on moon sighting or the lunar tithi).",
    "Section (ক) lists 15 general holidays (4 on weekly holidays) and section (খ) lists 14 executive-order holiday days (3 on weekly holidays). 2027-05-20 is both Buddha Purnima (general) and the third day after Eid-ul-Azha (executive order).",
    "Optional holidays: an employee may take at most 3 optional days per year according to their own religion, with prior approval obtained at the start of the year; optional days may be combined with general, executive-order and weekly holidays.",
    "Offices whose schedules and holidays are governed by their own laws, and offices or services declared essential, declare their own holidays in the public interest."
